            <h2 id="preparation">JPSC Prelims Preparation Strategy</h2>

            <p>
              A practical preparation cycle can be organized into seven
              stages. The order matters because each stage produces input for
              the next one.
            </p>

            <div class="timeline">
              <div class="timeline-item">
                <span>01</span>
                <div>
                  <h3>Read the syllabus</h3>
                  <p>
                    Convert every broad syllabus heading into a checklist of
                    concrete topics.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="timeline-item">
                <span>02</span>
                <div>
                  <h3>Analyse PYQs</h3>
                  <p>
                    Identify recurring themes, question styles and areas that
                    repeatedly demand attention.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="timeline-item">
                <span>03</span>
                <div>
                  <h3>Build the static foundation</h3>
                  <p>
                    Study History, Geography, Polity, Economy, Science and
                    Jharkhand-specific subjects systematically.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="timeline-item">
                <span>04</span>
                <div>
                  <h3>Maintain current affairs</h3>
                  <p>
                    Separate national/international current affairs from
                    Jharkhand current affairs so that state-specific revision
                    remains visible.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="timeline-item">
                <span>05</span>
                <div>
                  <h3>Revise repeatedly</h3>
                  <p>
                    Use short notes, topic checklists and error logs rather
                    than repeatedly rereading complete books.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="timeline-item">
                <span>06</span>
                <div>
                  <h3>Attempt mocks</h3>
                  <p>
                    Introduce timed tests before the final revision phase so
                    that speed and accuracy can be improved early.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="timeline-item">
                <span>07</span>
                <div>
                  <h3>Analyse every test</h3>
                  <p>
                    Record wrong answers, guessed answers, slow questions and
                    weak topics, then revise those areas.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="formula">
              <span>SYLLABUS</span>
              <b>+</b>
              <span>PYQs</span>
              <b>+</b>
              <span>REVISION</span>
              <b>+</b>
              <span>MOCKS</span>
              <b>=</b>
              <strong>EXAM-READY PREPARATION</strong>
            </div>

            <h2>JPSC Syllabus vs PYQs vs Mock Tests</h2>

            <div class="comparison-table">
