                <span>What JPSC has actually asked</span>
                <span>Find patterns and recurring themes</span>
              </div>

              <div class="comparison-row">
                <strong>Mock Tests</strong>
                <span>How prepared you are</span>
                <span>Measure score, accuracy, time and weaknesses</span>
              </div>
            </div>

            <h2>What Should You Study First?</h2>

            <p>
              Do not interpret question distribution as permission to ignore
              lower-weight areas. Instead, use the official distribution to
              create a priority order while still completing the complete
              syllabus.
            </p>

            <div class="priority-grid">
              <div class="priority-card high">
                <span>HIGH PRIORITY</span>
                <h3>History</h3>
                <p>15 questions in the published Paper-I distribution.</p>
              </div>

              <div class="priority-card high">
                <span>HIGH PRIORITY</span>
                <h3>Science &amp; Technology</h3>
                <p>15 questions in the published Paper-I distribution.</p>
              </div>

              <div class="priority-card high">
                <span>HIGH PRIORITY</span>
                <h3>Current Events</h3>
                <p>15 questions in the published Paper-I distribution.</p>
              </div>

              <div class="priority-card medium">
                <span>CORE</span>
